.TH ADA-QUALITY 1 "2026-11-19" "ada-quality 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ada-quality \- assess and report Ada project quality
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ada-quality
[global options] command [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ada Quality registers Ada projects, runs reproducible assessments, persists evidence, and exports text, JSON, SARIF, JUnit, and CSV reports.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B project
Add, discover, synchronize, list, show, enable, disable, relocate, remove, tag, or untag projects.
.TP
.B check, scan
Run a complete assessment or analyze selected changed source files.
.PP
Checks accept --jobs N for bounded parallelism, --reuse-unchanged for exact cache hits, --dry-run for a no-write
execution plan, --tag NAME, --profile NAME, and --project-policy. Scans accept --git-diff BASE and combinable
--staged, --unstaged, and --untracked modes.
.TP
.B assessment, history, findings, status, regressions, trend
Inspect assessments, aliases, portfolio state, comparisons, findings, and metric history. Project tags filter all
portfolio query surfaces; collection JSON includes a stable snapshot and an opaque next cursor accepted by --cursor.
.TP
.B report --format json
Export the archive. Use --project or --tag together with --since and --until to select a self-contained subset.
.TP
.B report --format html
Write a self-contained portfolio report, optionally with --output FILE.
.TP
.B policy
Initialize, validate, show, discover profiles, diff/impact two profiles, or render a project's effective policy. The
effective command accepts --explain to identify the document selecting every value.
.TP
.B database
Initialize, check, recover, compact, inspect, back up, export, import, restore, merge, sign, verify, or archive-and-prune the database.
.PP
database archive DEST --before UTC [--keep N] verifies a complete logical archive before removing eligible old
terminal assessments. Running assessments and the newest N terminal assessments per project are retained.
With --dry-run and no destination, the exact removal set is printed without changing the database.
.PP
database merge SOURCE... --dry-run reports the combined additions, reuse, aliases, and conflicts without writes.
Applied merges commit every source's registry, evidence, event, and alias changes in one transaction.
.PP
database keygen PRIVATE PUBLIC creates an Ed25519 keypair. backup and export accept --sign-key PRIVATE.
database verify accepts --public-key PUBLIC or --trust-store DIR. database inspect reads signature metadata, while
database trust add/list/remove manages stable key identities. restore and import accept either verification mode.
.TP
.B doctor, waiver audit
Diagnose policy, database, project, and tool availability, or inventory active, unused, expiring, expired, and
malformed source waivers. Portfolio selectors and configurable failure/expiry thresholds support CI use. Both
commands support versioned JSON.
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh|fish
Write a shell completion definition to standard output.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --database PATH
Select the database (default .ada-quality.db).
.TP
.B --policy PATH
Select the policy file (default quality-policy.toml).
.TP
.B --format FORMAT, --json
Select machine-readable output where supported.
.TP
.B --error-format text|json
Select human-readable or structured standard-error diagnostics.
.TP
.B --output FILE
Write read-command output to a file. Collection views also accept --limit N, --offset N, and --cursor TOKEN.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable terminal styling.
.SH STATUS FILTERS
Use --only unhealthy or --only regressed. Stale filtering requires --only stale together with --since UTC, and selects projects whose latest assessment predates that instant or has no timestamp.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means success. Assessment or scan violations return 1, usage errors 2, incomplete execution 3, and storage/reporting errors 4.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I quality-policy.toml
Default quality policy.
.TP
.I .ada-quality.db
Default persistent database.
